    "text": "The 4:10 from Ballarat was late again. I stood at the end of the platform with the cardboard sign Aunty Losa had made, MELE in purple marker, and tried not to feel silly holding it.\n\nI had not seen my cousin since we were six. Back then she had cried the whole way through my birthday party because a balloon popped near her ear. Mum said she had grown up a lot since, but I had my doubts. Someone who cried about balloons, I decided, would probably hate our noisy house.\n\nWhen the train finally pulled in, a tall girl with a guitar case jumped down before the doors had fully opened. She spotted the sign, laughed, and pointed at it.\n\n'You spelt it right this time,' she said.\n\nI had no idea what she meant until Mum told me in the car. At my sixth birthday, I had written her name on the cake myself, in icing, as MEL. She had not been crying about the balloon at all.",
